 "readme": "# Synthetic Data Lakehouse\n\nProduction pipeline: **real Kaggle/OpenAPI data** → medallion lakehouse → **SDV** synthetic data → **Ollama** validation → **Airflow** orchestration → **PySpark/Databricks** at scale.\n\n## Browser URLs (local Docker)\n\n| Service | URL | Login |\n|---------|-----|-------|\n| **Airflow** | http://localhost:8080 | admin / admin |\n| **Dashboard** | http://localhost:8501 | — |\n| **Ollama API** | http://localhost:11434 | — |\n| **Source Postgres** | localhost:5433 | source_user / source_pass |\n\n## One command to run everything\n\n```powershell\ncopy .env.example .env\nollama pull llama3.2\n\n# Full stack: Docker + fetch + ETL + synthetic + dashboard + open browser\n.\\run.ps1 -WithDocker -WithDashboard -OpenBrowser\n\n# Or without Docker (Ollama already running on host):\n.\\run.ps1 -WithDashboard\n```\n\nEquivalent:\n```powershell\npython run.py --with-docker --with-dashboard --open-browser\n```\n\n`run.py` steps automatically:\n1. Create `.env` if missing  \n2. Start Docker (optional) + wait for Ollama & Airflow  \n3. Fetch real data (OpenAPI/Kaggle)  \n4. Bronze → Silver → Gold → Ollama validation → SDV synthetic  \n5. Print results + start dashboard  \n\n| Flag | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| `--with-docker` | Start Airflow, Ollama, Postgres, Dashboard containers |\n| `--with-dashboard` | Keep Streamlit on http://localhost:8501 |\n| `--open-browser` | Open URLs when ready |\n| `--source kaggle` | Use Kaggle dataset |\n| `--skip-fetch` | Reuse existing landing data |\n\n---\n\n## Manual steps (optional)\n\n### Configure environment\n\n```powershell\ncopy .env.example .env\n# DATA_SOURCE=openapi | kaggle\n# OLLAMA_MOCK=false\n```\n\n### Browser URLs\n\n| Service | URL |\n|---------|-----|\n| **Airflow** | http://localhost:8080 (admin/admin) |\n| **Dashboard** | http://localhost:8501 |\n| **Ollama** | http://localhost:11434 |\n\n---\n\n## Data sources (`DATA_SOURCE`)\n\n| Value | Description | Credentials |\n|-------|-------------|-------------|\n| `openapi` | [Fake Store API](https://fakestoreapi.com) + [DummyJSON](https://dummyjson.com) users/carts | None |\n| `kaggle` | [carrie1/ecommerce-data](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/carrie1/ecommerce-data) Online Retail CSV | `KAGGLE_USERNAME` + `KAGGLE_KEY` |\n| `postgres` | Read from source DB after load | Docker `source-db` |\n\n```powershell\n# OpenAPI (default)\npython scripts/fetch_real_data.py --source openapi\n\n# Kaggle\n$env:KAGGLE_USERNAME=\"your_user\"\n$env:KAGGLE_KEY=\"your_key\"\npython scripts/fetch_real_data.py --source kaggle\n```\n\n---\n\n## Ollama (real, not mocked)\n\n- Set `OLLAMA_MOCK=false` in `.env`\n- `OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434` when Ollama runs on host\n- Inside Docker Airflow/dashboard: `http://ollama:11434`\n- If Ollama is on host but apps in Docker: `http://host.docker.internal:11434`\n\n```powershell\npython scripts/wait_for_ollama.py\npython scripts/run_local_pipeline.py\n```\n\n---\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\nOpenAPI / Kaggle / Postgres\n        ↓\n   Airflow 01_ingestion (fetch → validate)\n        ↓\n   Bronze → Silver → Gold (02_transformation)\n        ↓\n   Quality checks (04_quality_validation)\n        ↓\n   Ollama gate → SDV → Ollama validate (03_synthetic)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Project layout\n\n```\npipeline/data_sources/   # kaggle_loader, openapi_loader\ndashboard/app.py         # Streamlit UI :8501\ndocker/docker-compose.yml\nscripts/fetch_real_data.py\nscripts/run_local_pipeline.py\nscripts/start_stack.ps1\n```\n\n---\n\n## Tests\n\n```powershell\npytest tests/unit -q\n```\n\n## Windows + SDV\n\nIf PyTorch fails (`c10.dll`), the pipeline uses a statistical bootstrap synthesizer locally; use **Docker/Linux** for full CTGAN, or fix PyTorch CPU in `etl_env`.\n",
